  "id": "cluttering",
  "term": "cluttering",
  "definition": "Cluttering is a fluency disorder in which parts of a person’s speech in their native language are usually heard as excessively fast, irregular, or both. This description relies on the listener’s judgment and does not set exact cutoffs for how fast or irregular speech must be.",
